  "note": "Municipal election, 15 October 1937. Five nominations were received for five seats, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 October 1937, p. 9). The four retiring members (Carson, Dunseath, Pepper and Seery) were renominated; Thomas M'Candless filled the vacancy caused by Noel Taylor's resignation. Returned unopposed."
